Fillets and chamfers: a guide wholly before the spine's start, or wholly
past its end, is the spine's straight extension there (mitcad#1185).

The case: a plate whose top long edges are chamfered 2, its end then cut
round to a rounded octagon (45 degree sides, corners of radius 4). A
chamfer of 2 on one of the 45 degree top edges takes the chain of tangent
edges along the cut (diagonal, arc, end, arc, diagonal). Each diagonal
ends against the earlier chamfer's face, and beyond the diagonal's top
edge its vertical face goes on tangentially into a corner's cylinder. The
analytic pieces of the chain (ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd) run on past both ends
of the spine up to where the bevel's lower contact leaves the diagonal's
face; the rest, over the cylinder up to the earlier chamfer's face, is
walked. At the chain's end the walk's guide is the last edges and their
extension. At its start the guide lay wholly before the spine's start,
from the extension to the first piece's start, a parameter before the
first edge's start; ChFi3d_PerformElSpine trimmed the first edge from its
start to that parameter, a trim that ran backwards, and the guide doubled
back along the edge. The walk from the piece stalled within a hundredth
of a millimetre, the first sections of its piece were never set, and
ChFi3d_FilDS put the piece's point index into the DS as a vertex's: the
topological build read the solid as a vertex (TopoDS_Builder::Add).

Such a guide is now built as the spine's straight extension, as where an
analytic piece took the whole edge (the guide's "cepadur" case, already a
line through the guide's end along its tangent), at an end of the spine no
other blend meets: PerformSetOfKPart tells ChFi3d_PerformElSpine which
ends are free (its new StraightPastEnds). Where another blend meets the
spine at that vertex, the corner between them cuts what the walk makes
past it, and the guide stays as before: the diagonal chamfered together
with its edge on the earlier chamfer's face and the corner's edge there
(a corner of two chamfers at the diagonal's end) built before, and with a
guide on past the vertex its corner failed. The plate's chamfer builds
with both ends of the chain alike: valid, closed, its centre of mass on
the plate's plane of symmetry within 1e-9 mm.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
index 865a08f3..6e8099da 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
@@ -7011,7 +7011,8 @@ Standard_EXPORT void ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>& HES,
                                            occ::handle<ChFiDS_Spine>&   Spine,
                                            const GeomAbs_Shape          continuity,
                                            const double                 tol,
-                                           const bool                   IsOffset)
+                                           const bool                   IsOffset,
+                                           const int                    StraightPastEnds)
 {
 
   bool                           periodic, Bof, checkdeb, cepadur, bIsSmooth;
@@ -7212,6 +7213,26 @@ Standard_EXPORT void ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>& HES,
   {
     cepadur = true;
   }
+  // A guide wholly before the spine's start (or wholly past its end), at
+  // an end of the spine no other blend meets (StraightPastEnds: 1 its
+  // start, 2 its end): an analytic piece of the first edge was cut on
+  // beyond the spine's start (ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd) and the walk goes on
+  // from it into the extension. The edge has no part of the guide, and its
+  // trim from the edge's start to the guide's end, a parameter before that
+  // start, ran backwards: the guide doubled back along the edge, the walk
+  // from the piece stalled within a hundredth of a millimetre, and its
+  // piece's first sections were left unset (a chamfer ending against an
+  // earlier chamfer's face: the DS read the solid as a vertex,
+  // TopoDS_Builder::Add). The guide is the spine's straight extension
+  // there, as where a piece took the whole edge. (Where another blend meets
+  // the spine there, the corner between them cuts what the walk makes past
+  // the vertex: the guide is as before.)
+  if (!periodic && WF < WL
+      && ((WL < Spine->FirstParameter(1) + tol && (StraightPastEnds & 1) != 0)
+          || (WF > Spine->LastParameter(nbed) - tol && (StraightPastEnds & 2) != 0)))
+  {
+    cepadur = true;
+  }
   //
   // Petite veru pour les cas ou un KPart a bouffe l arete
   // sans parvenir a terminer. On tire une droite.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.hxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.hxx
index dce45a7b..3c1b6e5a 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.hxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.hxx
@@ -465,7 +465,8 @@ Standard_EXPORT void ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>& HES,
                                            occ::handle<ChFiDS_Spine>&   Spine,
                                            const GeomAbs_Shape          continuity,
                                            const double                 tol,
-                                           const bool                   IsOffset = false);
+                                           const bool                   IsOffset = false,
+                                           const int                    StraightPastEnds = 0);
 
 TopoDS_Face ChFi3d_EnlargeFace(const occ::handle<ChFiDS_Spine>&        Spine,
                                const occ::handle<BRepAdaptor_Surface>& HS,
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
index d71cd1cd..4c4a518f 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -18897,18 +18897,39 @@ void ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfKPart(occ::handle<ChFiDS_Stripe>& Stripe, const
     }
   }
 
+  // The ends of the spine no other blend meets: a guide wholly past such an
+  // end is the spine's straight extension (ChFi3d_PerformElSpine).
+  int aFreeEnds = 0;
+  if (!Spine->IsPeriodic())
+  {
+    for (int k = 0; k < 2; k++)
+    {
+      const TopoDS_Vertex aV    = k == 0 ? Spine->FirstVertex() : Spine->LastVertex();
+      bool                aMeet = aV.IsNull();
+      for (NCollection_List<occ::handle<ChFiDS_Stripe>>::Iterator it(myListStripe); it.More() && !aMeet; it.Next())
+      {
+        const occ::handle<ChFiDS_Spine>& aSp = it.Value()->Spine();
+        aMeet = it.Value() != Stripe && !aSp.IsNull()
+                && (aSp->FirstVertex().IsSame(aV) || aSp->LastVertex().IsSame(aV));
+      }
+      if (!aMeet)
+      {
+        aFreeEnds |= k == 0 ? 1 : 2;
+      }
+    }
+  }
   NCollection_List<occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>>&          ll = Spine->ChangeElSpines();
   NCollection_List<occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>>::Iterator ILES(ll);
   for (; ILES.More(); ILES.Next())
   {
-    ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(ILES.ChangeValue(), Spine, myConti, tolesp);
+    ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(ILES.ChangeValue(), Spine, myConti, tolesp, false, aFreeEnds);
   }
   if (Spine->Mode() == ChFiDS_ConstThroatWithPenetrationChamfer)
   {
     NCollection_List<occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>>& offsetll = Spine->ChangeOffsetElSpines();
     for (ILES.Initialize(offsetll); ILES.More(); ILES.Next())
     {
-      ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(ILES.ChangeValue(), Spine, myConti, tolesp, true);
+      ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(ILES.ChangeValue(), Spine, myConti, tolesp, true, aFreeEnds);
     }
   }
   Spine->SplitDone(true);
